## 1.6.0
- Map: restart and reset times name the viewer's time zone (they were already in the viewer's local time)
- Public info page (Settings → Public info): the server's settings in plain words and groups, game rules, data pack settings and the mod configs you pick (as readable lists), with search; at /info/ or on its own domain with INFO_HOST. Passwords, tokens and remote-access settings never show; it stays readable while the server is off
- Settings → Server list: a collection of messages of the day; tick the ones to use and a random one is picked at every start
- Maintenance: who may join is a list of known players (operators, whitelist, everyone who has joined) with checkboxes, plus a field to add names
- Performance → Tuning: merging, breeding caps and trading halls are separate cards; settings whose switch is off are greyed out; one save bar stays at hand
- Cards fold by clicking their title, like on the dashboard pages; "Day by day" is a normal card and starts folded
- Text fields and selects have the same height everywhere, selects with their own arrow
- No more flicker on reload: the icon font loads early, the panel logo stays cached and shows from the first frame, the clock badge only redraws when it changes
- More flavor: each area has its own colour (sidebar, page icon, card icons), a greeting banner on Home with the server list message and how the server is doing, a soft brand glow with a faint block grid behind the pages, gradient primary buttons

## 1.5.0
- New navigation: 13 areas in the sidebar (Home, Console, Players, Performance, World, Settings, Schedule, Backups, Files, Updates, Users & roles, Discord, Appearance, Audit log) with sub-tabs for related pages, a page title and a sentence on what each page is for; links like #world/map open a page directly
- Quick search (Ctrl/⌘ K or the search field in the sidebar) jumps to any page or setting
- Home: "Needs attention" (crash, failed backups and tasks, disk almost full, maintenance on, mod updates) and a setup checklist
- Performance → Tuning: dynamic distances, entity activation range, merge radius, breeding caps, villagers in trading cells, cleanup of items and excess mobs, and the laggiest chunks with Freeze/Unfreeze
- Players → Maintenance: staff-only mode with its own server list message and icon, kick countdown; also as a scheduled step
- Settings → Server list: MOTD with colour buttons and a live preview, server icon upload (scaled to 64 × 64)
- Schedule: Clean up and Maintenance steps
- Whitelist & bans lists who's online with Kick and Ban; the Players page no longer has its own Kick/Ban buttons
- Public map: a status card with online/offline/maintenance, players, uptime over 7 days, the next restart and the next outer wilds reset, plus the in-game date and time from the Nice Actions calendar (each can be switched off, names optional)
- Account and Log out moved to a menu under your name in the navbar; expert Java settings are folded under "Advanced"
- Cleaner look: Inter instead of Montserrat (kept for the wordmark), one type scale, lighter weights, calmer card titles and buttons, fewer all-caps labels
- Borders: "Show soft border" per dimension draws the permanent area's edge as green particles for players near it (a round hard border as red ones)
- Map: clicking a waypoint shows its owner's head and its subtitle (descriptions and names set as text components now show too)
- Stats: steps of the dynamic distances show as markers, and the day table counts them ("Lag steps")
- The "Trimming…" line goes away when the reset is done and shows its outcome; an aborted upload no longer leaves its progress box
- Maintenance mode no longer writes its message into server.properties (the normal MOTD stays as you set it, even after a crash); server.properties is read as UTF-8 like Minecraft writes it, so § and other non-ASCII text show correctly
- Discord: events for dynamic distance steps (alerts channel, off by default) and maintenance on/off

## 1.4.3
- Startup: the Generational ZGC preset adds -XX:SoftMaxHeapSize (7/8 of the maximum memory, e.g. 14G of 16G) and is the default for new installs, listed first
- Discord: choose per event whether it posts in the chat channel or the alerts channel; by default chat, joins, leaves, deaths, advancements and online/offline go to chat, and lag, crashes and failures go to alerts

## 1.4.2
- Whitelist & bans: tick several actions for one player at once (whitelist, operator with level, ban with reason); IP bans have their own row
- The lists follow changes made in game or in the console (/op, /deop, /ban, /whitelist) while the page is open
- The panel logo also shows on the login screen
- Phones: the navbar scrolls away instead of covering a third of the screen

## 1.4.1
- No more automatic backups before every action: resetting the outer wilds, restoring a backup and updating Minecraft each have a "Back up first" box (also on the scheduled reset step). Without one, a failed update puts the old mods and server jar back; Undo is offered for updates that made a backup
- Resetting the outer wilds: no preview map any more, "Check what would go" tells the numbers; step logs (updates, resets) are a clean checklist with the current step and the outcome highlighted
- Console: filter by All, Errors, Warnings, Nice Control Center or Panel, and show or hide debug lines (stack traces stay with their error)
- Stats: "Day by day" table, one row per day (online time, TPS, MSPT, slowest tick, peak players, crashes, peak memory, free disk); a day opens to its hours
- Map: the logo replaces the title and is centered; "the outer wilds reset tomorrow" counts calendar days
- Power buttons that don't apply right now are faded

## 1.4.0
- One navigation for everything: a sidebar with groups (Dashboard, Live, Players, World, Server, Admin) holds the panel's pages and the mod dashboard's pages; the second tab bar is gone, the mod's pages open inside the panel at full height, and its badges show in the sidebar. On phones the sidebar slides in from a menu button
- The navbar holds the server state with its uptime, the in-game clock, Start/Restart/Stop/Kill and the stat tiles (TPS, MSPT, CPU, memory, disk, GC, entities, chunks, players) on every page; the big "Server running" box is gone, and notices (crash, restart countdown) show as a slim line only when there is one
- Replies from players (/nccreply) show as a message in the corner on every page; clicking one opens the conversation
- Console and Schedule exist only once: the mod's copies are hidden; tasks still in the mod's own schedule are listed in Schedule and can be moved over with one click
- Files: New file; files open in their own editor window with syntax highlighting (JSON, YAML, TOML, properties and more), search, and the form view for simple configs; right-click a file or folder for open, download, copy path, rename, duplicate, zip, extract and delete; drag and drop works anywhere in the Files page, also whole folders; uploads continue in the background with progress on every page
- Backups: one number for how many to keep (pinned ones come on top); what to leave out is picked in a folder tree, wildcard patterns still possible
- Scheduled messages and countdowns: {time}, {player} (each reader's own name), {online}, {clock}, {date} and & color codes, with clickable chips to insert them
- Borders & reset: the switches in the borders table work
- Stats: the charts fill their rows without gaps and size to their space
- Appearance (new): upload a logo for the panel (replaces the "Nice Control Center" lettering) and one for the public map
- Map: no seams at region borders anymore (the relief along each region's edge uses the region next to it), smoother zoomed-out tiles, crisp blocks when zoomed in; existing maps are drawn again once by themselves

## 1.3.0
- New Stats tab: TPS, milliseconds per tick, players, memory and free disk over 24 hours to 90 days, with starts, stops, crashes and alerts marked, a disk-full forecast and the busiest times per weekday and hour (kept in /data/panel/stats, no database needed)
- New Players tab: whitelist, operators, banned players and IPs; changes go through the console while the server runs and into the files while it's stopped
- Discord alerts for admins, optionally in their own channel: lag (needs mod 1.6.0), failed scheduled tasks and backups, outer wilds reset, disk almost full, memory pressure; crash messages name the mod that probably caused it. Alerts also show in the panel's console
- The web map shows the soft and hard borders and when the outer wilds reset next
- Pregenerate: choose to slow down, pause or keep going while players are online (also for the schedule step)
- Copy, zip and unzip in Files, and the trim preview, run in the background with progress instead of inside the request; trims plan in the background too; the version check hashes mod jars in parallel

## 1.2.0
- World tab: borders per dimension in one table (shape, center, soft border, hard border, pregenerate on/off, world border on/off), replacing the single area form; the permanent area inside the soft border is never trimmed, the outer wilds between soft and hard border can be reset
- Pregenerate goes up to the hard border in every dimension with Pregen on, one after another, optionally only the outer wilds (needs mod 1.5.0)
- "Reset the outer wilds" trims outside the soft border in every dimension with borders, with one backup; the preview map shows the hard border as a dashed line
- New schedule steps "Reset the outer wilds" (countdown in chat, stops the server, trims, starts it again) and "Pregenerate", and a "Weekly outer wilds reset" preset

## 1.1.0
- Discord messages relayed into the game also show in the console log and the dashboard's new Chat tab (needs mod 1.4.0; older mods still get them as before, only in game)
- The dashboard's Chat tab needs "console.read" to see and "console.write" to send, like the console

## 1.0.1
- Minecraft updates swap the Nice Control Center mod for the build made for the new version (before, the old build stayed because all builds share a version number, Fabric refused to start and the update rolled back); the mod is now saved as nice-control-center-<version>-mc<minecraft>.jar
- Typing stop in the console (or /stop in game) stops the server instead of counting as a crash and restarting it
- No automatic crash restart can start the server while a backup is restored or the world is trimmed
- Unzipping works in the server folder itself; each entry is checked, so nothing lands in the running world or outside the folder
- Zipping a folder into a zip inside it no longer packs the zip into itself
- The login limit and the audit log use the client address the reverse proxy reports, which a client can't fake with its own X-Forwarded-For header
- The public map sends no players, claims or hubs of hidden dimensions
- Log cleanup rules can't point at the server folder itself or the world
- Versions: version numbers and Modrinth file names are checked before they become file names
- Discord: the login check waits at most 1.5 s for Discord, and a missing webhook permission isn't asked again on every chat line
- `./gradlew build` works again for the panel (the plain jar is now ...-plain.jar)

## 1.0.0
First full release. The panel runs one Fabric server in Docker and manages it from outside:
- Server: start, stop, restart, kill, live console, crash detection with automatic restarts, Java and memory settings
- Accounts: users with roles and fine-grained permissions, audit log, container admin that always works
- Dashboard: the Nice Control Center mod's performance dashboard inside the panel, installed and updated automatically
- Backups with exclusions, retention, pinning, download and selective restore; scheduled tasks with countdown restarts
- Files in the browser, config editor with syntax checks and form view, SFTP with SSH keys, log cleanup
- Versions: Fabric Loader and Minecraft updates with a Modrinth mod check, automatic rollback and undo
- Discord bridge: linking required to play, chat both ways, event messages, bot status
- Web map with players, claims, waypoint hubs and the world border, on its own address if wanted
- World: pregeneration and a Chunky-style trim with a preview on the map
- Minecraft 26.1 to 26.3

## 0.10.0
- World tab: one area (dimension, center, radius, square or circle; fill in from the world border or spawn) for pregenerating and trimming
- Pregenerate: every chunk in the area, in a spiral from the center, only as fast as the server has room for, also with nobody online; progress, speed and time left (needs the Nice Control Center mod 1.2.1)
- Trim outside the area like Chunky: whole region files outside, single chunks along the edge (files packed again so the space is freed), entities and points of interest too; optionally keeps chunks players spent time in
- Trim preview on the map: the edge in green, what goes in red (only for accounts allowed to trim, never on the public map)
- Trimming only while the server is stopped, always after a backup; the server can't be started while it runs; the map redraws afterwards

## 0.9.0
- Web map: drawn by the panel from the region files (no load on the server, stays online while it's off), one pixel per block like a vanilla map with relief and water depth, zoomable from 1:1 out to 16,384 blocks per tile
- Live layers from the mod: online players with their heads, GOML claims, Explorer's Eden waypoint hubs (public ones by default), the world border; the last claims and hubs stay visible while the server is off
- Modded blocks get their real map colors once the server has run with the mod; until then vanilla colors are built in
- Its own address with MAP_HOST (e.g. map.example.com): there only the map is reachable, nothing of the panel
- Map tab: on/off, title, which layers and dimensions are shown, draw everything again
- Works with 26.x worlds (new block palette format) and older ones
- New permissions: set up the map; trim and pregenerate the world (used by the world trimmer)

## 0.8.0
- Discord bridge: players must link a Discord account to play (a code from the join screen, sent to the bot by direct message; optional: must still be on the Discord server; operators and a list of names can skip it)
- Chat both ways: game chat to a channel with the player's name and head, Discord messages into the game (chat only, never commands; mentions can't ping)
- Event messages for joins, leaves, deaths, advancements, server online/offline and crashes, each switchable with its own text
- The bot's status shows whether the server is up and how many play
- Linked accounts list with unlink; players can send "unlink" to the bot
- Needs the Nice Control Center mod 1.2.0 (installed automatically) for the login check and game events
- New permission: Discord bridge and linked accounts

## 0.7.0
- Versions: see the installed Minecraft and Fabric Loader, update Fabric Loader with one click when a newer one is out, or move to another Minecraft version (26.x by default, snapshots and older ones on request)
- Mod check on Modrinth for the target version: works, update available, no version yet, not on Modrinth; also flags mods that need a newer Fabric Loader; choose per mod: update, keep or turn off
- Every update: backup first, download and verify, stop, swap the server jar and mods, start; if the server doesn't come up, the backup is restored automatically
- Undo for the last update; history of all updates
- Backups an update or restore still needs are never removed by retention
- New permission: update Fabric and Minecraft

## 0.6.0
- Files: browse the server folder, upload (also by drag & drop, with progress), download (folders as zip), rename/move, copy, zip, unzip, new folder, delete to a 7-day trash
- Edit text files in the panel with line numbers; the world folder is read-only while the server runs
- Configs: every file in config/, grouped by mod, with a syntax check before saving (JSON, JSON5, TOML, YAML, properties) that points to the line of the problem; simple files also as a form (switches, numbers, text), keeping comments and layout; the previous version stays as .bak
- SFTP on port 2022 with the panel accounts: password or SSH keys (added under Account), read-only without write permission, can't leave the server folder, uploads/renames/deletes in the audit log
- Log cleanup: delete old files in logs, crash-reports and debug by age, with a preview; runs daily after 05:00
- New permissions: browse/download files, change files, edit mod configs (only config/), SFTP

## 0.5.0
- Backups: zip files of the server folder, made while the server runs (saving pauses for the copy, so the world is consistent); region files are stored as they are, the rest is compressed quickly
- Leave folders and files out with patterns (logs, caches, map renders, …), keep the newest N plus one per day and per week, pin backups to keep them forever
- Download backups, and restore all or only chosen folders/files while the server is stopped (a safety backup is made first)
- Scheduled tasks: at set times on chosen weekdays or every few minutes; steps: restart after a countdown in chat, stop, start, backup, console command, chat message, wait
- Templates for a daily restart at 04:00 (backup first, 5-minute countdown) and a backup every 6 hours; run any task now
- New permissions: see/download backups, make backups, restore/delete/pin backups and change backup settings; Moderators may see and make backups
- TIMEZONE (e.g. Europe/Berlin) for schedules and backup names

## 0.4.0
- Dashboard tab: the Nice Control Center mod's full dashboard (performance, world, players, server, data packs, updates, schedule, reports) inside the panel, with the panel's accounts
- New permissions for it: see the dashboard, manage players, change server settings (server.properties, game rules, data pack settings), manage updates, edit scheduled commands; Moderator and Viewer get sensible defaults
- Every change made in the dashboard goes to the audit log
- Installs the Nice Control Center mod for the server's Minecraft version and keeps it up to date before each start (can be switched off under Startup & Java)
- PANEL_PUBLIC_URL: /ncc web in the game links to the panel's Dashboard tab

## 0.3.0
- User accounts in Postgres (DB_URL, DB_USER, DB_PASS); the panel creates and updates its tables itself
- Roles with permissions: Admin (everything), Moderator and Viewer built in and adjustable, plus your own roles
- Permissions per action: see the server, power actions, read and run console commands, change Java settings, manage users, read the audit log; the UI only shows what an account may do
- Audit log of logins (also failed ones), server actions, console commands, settings changes and account changes, with search
- Change your own password; changing, disabling or deleting an account logs it out everywhere at once
- Sessions are kept in the database (survive panel restarts); passwords are Argon2id hashes
- The container admin (PANEL_ADMIN_USER / PANEL_ADMIN_PASSWORD) can always log in, also while the database is down
- Tabs: Console, Startup & Java, Users, Audit log, Account

## 0.2.0
- Runs the Minecraft server: start, stop, restart and kill, with the state, uptime and PID in the header
- Live console over a WebSocket, with search and a command line
- Crash detection (unexpected exit, crash report name) and automatic restart after 10 s, 30 s, 2 min, then 10 min; gives up after 5 crashes in 15 minutes
- Starts the server when the panel starts, and stops it cleanly when the container stops
- Startup & Java settings: memory, garbage collector flags (Aikar's G1 or generational ZGC), extra flags, Java runtime and server jar, with a preview of the command line
- EULA prompt before the first start
- Login for one admin (PANEL_ADMIN_USER / PANEL_ADMIN_PASSWORD, or a generated password printed once in the log)

## 0.1.0
- First skeleton: the panel starts in Docker, serves its start page in the dashboard's style and answers a health check
